diff -ruN a/crates/mtg-cards/cards/deps-reviewed.txt b/crates/mtg-cards/cards/deps-reviewed.txt
--- a/crates/mtg-cards/cards/deps-reviewed.txt	2026-10-06 06:23:34.199951149 +0000
+++ b/crates/mtg-cards/cards/deps-reviewed.txt	2026-10-06 06:23:34.203605008 +0000
@@ -4,3 +4,4 @@
 # Review 2026-10-01 (implementer; a second reader should confirm before the core freeze).
 Kaito, Bane of Nightmares | Magus of the Moon | L4 | independent: Kaito's type change applies only to Kaito, a planeswalker that is never a land, and Magus applies only to nonbasic lands; neither changes whether the other applies. Breaks only if a pool card could make Kaito a land or make a land a Kaito.
 Magus of the Moon | Overlord of the Balemurk | L4 | independent: Overlord's "isn't a creature while it has time counters" applies only to itself, never a land; Magus's affected set (nonbasic lands) and result (Mountain, no abilities) are the same in either order.
+Emblem: Tezzeret robots | Magus of the Moon | L4 | independent: the emblem only adds the Creature type and the Robot subtype to an artifact (it never adds or removes Land), and Magus of the Moon applies to nonbasic lands and turns them into Mountains; whether Magus applies depends on the Land type and the basic supertype, which the emblem leaves alone, and Magus's result (subtypes, lost abilities) does not change whether the emblem's target is an artifact. Breaks only if a pool card could remove the Land type or the Artifact type in layer 4.
